<title>USA: Israel's MER Telemanagement IPO moved to next year.</title>
<headline>Israel's MER Telemanagement IPO moved to next year.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The planned initial public offering of Israel's MER Telemanagement Inc has been moved until next year, according to lead underwriter Jefferies &amp; Co.</p>
<p>The company, which makes call management systems, is planning a $20 million initial public offering.  The deal had at one point been tentatively scheduled for this week, but is now slated for early next year.</p>
<p>The company is planning to offer two million shares for between $9 and $11 each, according to a regulatory filing.</p>
